        "_comment": "Frozen-valve variant of piecewise_Chamber_and_Valve.json: every PiecewiseValve sets freeze_state, so its resistance is decided once per driver step from the previous converged state instead of at every Newton iteration. Reduced from 30 cardiac cycles to 1 because lagging the valve switch by one step is destabilizing on this model: at 30 cycles the nonlinear solve fails at t=0.98 even with maximum_nonlinear_iterations raised to 100, and refining the time step makes it fail sooner, not later (fails at t=0.26 with 2000 pts/cycle, t=0.23 with 5000). This case therefore pins the frozen code path against its own output; it is not a check that freezing reproduces the unfrozen solution. For that see test_valve_freeze.py, which verifies frozen and unfrozen agree exactly when the valve does not switch."
    },
